# /etc/openexchange/cluster-tools/<worker>.env (ct-bridge.env, ct-forwarder.env): the worker's own settings, which
# it reads and checks itself (every problem listed in one pass, exit 78). See the worker's README section for the
# full list (BRIDGE_* for ct-bridge, FWD_* for ct-forwarder). The driver mode is not set here: the unit names it
# (ct-worker@ external, ct-worker-embedded@ embedded) and worker-launch refuses an env file that says otherwise.
#
# Embedded only: the parent of the in-process driver's directory (an existing, writable directory).
#BRIDGE_DRIVER_DIR=/dev/shm
#
# Memory and CPU: a taskset CPU list for the worker (read by worker-launch). Empty: unpinned.
CPU_SET=
#
# Credentials go in <worker>.secrets.env (root:root 0600), for example ME_AUTH_CREDENTIAL and CORE_AUTH_CREDENTIAL.
